                        "entry_id": "74c0b1cd-7258-3612-bb34-8d4f25d06df7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "black, Asian, and minority ethnic (“黑人、亞裔及[其他]少數族裔”) 之首字母縮略詞"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "form-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee5f36a5-c898-4173-98d8-18856470b8a8",
                                "sense_id": "24f15e46-4bd5-38f3-99a2-d73869886e89",
                                "text": "\"It's useful in that it promotes a kind of solidarity between the people that come under it belong to a BAME background, but it does lack nuance.",
                                "translation": "“它的优点在于促进了属于少数族裔背景的人们之间的团结，但它确实缺乏细致入微的考量。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e1621a1-1cbb-4d55-90db-e1cf58022a0f",
                                "sense_id": "24f15e46-4bd5-38f3-99a2-d73869886e89",
                                "text": "Ryan, Pollock and Antonelli (2009) reported that several teachers in Canada ‘struggle’ to interact with students of BAME origin who were often ‘othered’, in particular, those of migrant origin.",
                                "translation": "Ryan, Pollock 和 Antonelli (2009) 报告称，加拿大的一些教师在与少数族裔学生互动时“感到困难” ，这些学生经常被“视为异类”，尤其是移民出身的学生。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6cd92e94-847a-4b7c-837c-decc8077a380",
                                "sense_id": "24f15e46-4bd5-38f3-99a2-d73869886e89",
                                "text": "Ironically, there is some evidence that BAME parents want white teachers and leaders for their children, a form of ‘reverse racism’, suggesting that neocolonial attitudes persist through different generations.",
                                "translation": "具有讽刺意味的是，一些证据表明，少数族裔父母希望他们的孩子拥有白人教师和领导者，这是一种“反向种族主义”，表明新殖民主义态度在不同的世代中持续存在。"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
